Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم وصلوات الله والسلام عليه اجمعين.

38
00:01:34,389 --> 00:01:41,248
أو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَدَى ٱللَّهُ ۖ فَبِهُدَىٰهُمُ ٱقْتَدِهْ

39
00:01:41,513 --> 00:01:45,791
They are those, whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance.

40
00:01:47,307 --> 00:01:49,265
THE LIVES OF THE PROPHETS

41
00:01:50,396 --> 00:01:52,350
أعوذ بالله من الشيطان الرجيم ۞

42
00:01:52,451 --> 00:01:54,232
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ۞

43
00:01:55,015 --> 00:01:59,055
إن الحمد لله، نحمده ونستعينه ونستغفره ونستهديه،

44
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:03,314
 ونعوذ بالله من شرور أنفسنا ومن سيئات أعمالنا،

45
00:02:03,695 --> 00:02:07,560
من يهده الله فلا مضل له ومن يضلل فلا هادي له،

46
00:02:07,624 --> 00:02:13,695
وأشهد أن لا إله إلا الله وحده لا شريك له وأشهد أن محمداً عبده ورسوله،

47
00:02:13,814 --> 00:02:18,135
وأدى الأمانة , ونصح الأمة , وجاهد في الله حق جهاده،

48
00:02:18,518 --> 00:02:19,586
امَّا بعد

49
00:02:19,891 --> 00:02:22,992
فانَّ اَصدق الحديث كتاب الله وخير الهدي،

50
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:25,635
 هدي محمدٍ صلى الله عليه وسلم

51
00:02:25,984 --> 00:02:29,258
وشرَّ الأمورِ محدثاتُها وكلَّ محدثتٍ بدعةٍ ،

52
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:32,766
وكل بدعة ضلالةٌ ، وكلَّ ضلالةٍ في النارِ

53
00:02:33,091 --> 00:03:04,944
نَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ أَحْسَنَ ٱلْقَصَصِ بِمَآ أَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَيْكَ هَـٰذَا ٱلْقُرْءَانَ وَإِن كُنتَ مِن قَبْلِهِۦ لَمِنَ ٱلْغَـٰفِلِينَ۞

54
00:03:06,412 --> 00:03:07,862
Allah سبحانه وتعالى ‎says;

55
00:03:08,238 --> 00:03:16,273
We relate unto you, O Muhammad(محمد), the best of stories through Our revelations unto you of this Qur'an,

56
00:03:16,583 --> 00:03:20,131
and before this, you were among those who weren’t aware of it.

57
00:03:20,892 --> 00:03:22,123
It is from Allah.

58
00:03:23,464 --> 00:03:28,767
Allah سبحانه وتعالى is the One, Who is revealing this to Muhammad ﷺ and to this Ummah(أمة‎).

59
00:03:29,513 --> 00:03:31,601
نَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ أَحْسَنَ ٱلْقَصَصِ

60
00:03:31,641 --> 00:03:34,899
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى says: We relate unto you the best of stories.

61
00:03:35,451 --> 00:03:39,356
These are the best of stories because they are dealing with the best of creation.

62
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:45,137
Some of the benefits of talking about the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء);

63
00:03:45,214 --> 00:03:46,097
Number 1;

64
00:03:46,801 --> 00:03:49,896
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ was commanded to do so.

65
00:03:51,428 --> 00:03:52,531
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

66
00:03:52,587 --> 00:03:54,031
فَٱقْصُصِ ٱلْقَصَصَ

67
00:03:54,968 --> 00:03:57,158
Relate unto them the stories.

68
00:03:57,857 --> 00:04:01,203
It's a command from Allah سبحانه وتعالى given to Rasool Allah ﷺ

69
00:04:01,891 --> 00:04:08,915
Allah سبحانه وتعالى is commanding him that, you must narrate these stories unto the Ummah(امة).

70
00:04:10,534 --> 00:04:13,518
So, it becomes a duty upon us to relate these stories.

71
00:04:13,923 --> 00:04:20,147
It becomes mandatory on us to convey the message of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى and their stories.

72
00:04:20,972 --> 00:04:26,492
So number 1, we are doing this as a Ibadah(عبادة) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى, to fulfill a commandment of Allah.

73
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,511
Number 2;

74
00:04:29,463 --> 00:04:30,632
لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ۝

75
00:04:30,797 --> 00:04:36,002
فَٱقْصُصِ ٱلْقَصَصَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ۝

76
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:38,503
Relate and convey to them the stories.

77
00:04:38,543 --> 00:04:39,264
Why?

78
00:04:40,010 --> 00:04:41,276
So that they may reflect.

79
00:04:42,272 --> 00:04:43,730
لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ۝

80
00:04:43,916 --> 00:04:45,408
 So they may contemplate.

81
00:04:46,289 --> 00:04:47,225
Al-Tafakkur(التفكر)

82
00:04:47,765 --> 00:04:50,606
these stories are not to entertain us.

83
00:04:51,092 --> 00:04:53,992
These stories are for us to derive lessons, and reflect,

84
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:58,974
and to contemplate, and to think about, to deeply reflect on them,

85
00:04:59,109 --> 00:05:00,616
 that is what we need to do.

86
00:05:02,194 --> 00:05:03,292
Number 3;

87
00:05:04,212 --> 00:05:10,730
Another reason why it's extremely important to study the stories of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

88
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,373
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says:

89
00:05:12,643 --> 00:05:20,881
أُوْلَـٰئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَدَى ٱللَّهُ فَبِهُدَاهُمُ ٱقْتَدِهْ

90
00:05:21,349 --> 00:05:25,659
They are those, whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance.

91
00:05:26,992 --> 00:05:28,594
They are the ones who are guided,

92
00:05:29,427 --> 00:05:35,330
and Allah سبحانه وتعالى is instructing Rasool Allah ﷺ to follow them, to follow their guidance,

93
00:05:36,092 --> 00:05:37,727
because they are the best.

94
00:05:38,068 --> 00:05:39,126
We need to have role models.

95
00:05:39,219 --> 00:05:44,485
It is very important for the human being to have models, especially in the early stages of our life.

96
00:05:45,271 --> 00:05:49,263
You find that every human being has role models

97
00:05:49,909 --> 00:05:51,718
if they are not good, they're gonna be bad.

98
00:05:52,877 --> 00:05:56,081
That is our make-up as human beings;

99
00:05:56,369 --> 00:06:00,182
we must have some role models, we must have some people whom we look up to.

100
00:06:01,349 --> 00:06:08,694
If we’re not going to provide our children and our youth with the role models of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)

101
00:06:09,083 --> 00:06:13,098
and the role models of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the role models of the Sahabah(صحابه),

102
00:06:13,186 --> 00:06:17,923
they’re gonna find role models somewhere else, because human beings cannot live without role models.

103
00:06:20,479 --> 00:06:26,555
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى is telling Muhammad ﷺ that he must follow the way of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

104
00:06:26,809 --> 00:06:30,651
If this instruction was given to Rasool Allah ﷺ, then what should we do?

105
00:06:32,062 --> 00:06:33,742
فَبِهُدَىٰهُمُ ٱقْتَدِهْ

106
00:06:34,157 --> 00:06:37,329
Allah سبحانه وتعالى is commanding Rasool Allah ﷺ to follow their way.

107
00:06:38,353 --> 00:06:41,609
So we need to study the lives of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى

108
00:06:41,649 --> 00:06:43,702
so that they can become our role models.

109
00:06:45,246 --> 00:06:46,375
Number 4;

110
00:06:47,557 --> 00:06:48,542
TO LOVE THEM.

111
00:06:49,285 --> 00:06:50,235
Al-Mahabbah(المحبة).

112
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:54,091
If you do not know someone, you cannot love him.

113
00:06:55,798 --> 00:06:58,449
We all claim that we love the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah.

114
00:07:00,330 --> 00:07:02,543
But if we don't know the details of their life,

115
00:07:03,710 --> 00:07:06,710
we don't know what they went through,

116
00:07:07,487 --> 00:07:11,289
how could we have respect for them?

117
00:07:11,844 --> 00:07:15,067
Abu Dharr(أبوذر) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and asked him a question.

118
00:07:15,471 --> 00:07:17,331
قال كم عدة الأنبياء؟

119
00:07:18,177 --> 00:07:19,915
What is the total number of Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)?

120
00:07:22,218 --> 00:07:23,920
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

121
00:07:24,571 --> 00:07:32,351
مائة وعشرون ألفا الرسل من ذلك ثلاثمائة وخمسة عشر جما غفيرا

122
00:07:33,629 --> 00:07:35,018
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

123
00:07:35,224 --> 00:07:36,962
What is the number of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)?

124
00:07:37,621 --> 00:07:43,460
120,000 and the messengers among them are 315.

125
00:07:44,888 --> 00:07:48,358
So the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى are 120,000

126
00:07:49,810 --> 00:07:53,588
and the messengers, Al-Rusul(الرسل), are 315.

127
00:07:55,068 --> 00:08:00,231
I’m translating Nabi(نبي) as “Prophet” and Rasool(رسول) as “Messenger”.

128
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:05,353
So there are two different things, Nabi(نبي) and Rasool(رسول);

129
00:08:06,710 --> 00:08:09,616
Nabi (نبي), the plural of it is Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

130
00:08:10,155 --> 00:08:12,704
Rasool(رسول), the plural of it is Rusul(رسل).

131
00:08:13,553 --> 00:08:15,950
So what is the difference between the Nabi(نبي) and the Rasool(رسول)?

132
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:19,387
What is the difference between the Prophet and the Messenger?

133
00:08:19,775 --> 00:08:21,813
There are a few opinions of the Ulema(علماء‎) in this;

134
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:29,051
one of them is that the Rasool(رسول) is the Nabi(نبي) who is given a law.

135
00:08:31,795 --> 00:08:35,414
The Rasool(رسول) is a Nabi(نبي) who is given a law,

136
00:08:36,779 --> 00:08:42,821
but the Nabi(نبي) who is not a Rasool(رسول) is following the law of another Rasool(رسول).

137
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:47,684
So every Rasool(رسول) is a Nabi(نبي), but not every Nabi(نبي) is a Rasool(رسول).

138
00:08:47,915 --> 00:08:53,359
Every Prophet is not a Messenger, but every Messenger is a Prophet.

139
00:08:53,732 --> 00:08:58,131
If a Prophet is given a new law, then he becomes a Rasool(رسول) and a Nabi(نبي).

140
00:08:59,234 --> 00:09:03,449
If he’s not given a new law, then he is a Nabi(نبي) - only a Prophet.

141
00:09:03,862 --> 00:09:09,687
An example of that to make it little bit clearer Musa(موسی) is a Rasool(رسول).

142
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,277
Musa(موسی) is a Rasool(رسول).

143
00:09:12,362 --> 00:09:12,815
Why?

144
00:09:12,855 --> 00:09:14,906
Because he was given the Tawrah(توراة‎).

145
00:09:15,331 --> 00:09:18,285
But Harun(هارون) is not a Rasool(رسول),

146
00:09:18,373 --> 00:09:20,563
 Harun(هارون) is a Nabi(نبي).

147
00:09:20,873 --> 00:09:21,778
Why?

148
00:09:22,309 --> 00:09:25,040
Because he is following the law of his brother.

149
00:09:25,858 --> 00:09:28,588
Harun(هارون) is following the law of Musa(موسی).

150
00:09:29,390 --> 00:09:34,219
This is one difference that the Ulema(علماء‎) gave to between Nabi(نبي) and Rasool(رسول).

151
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:42,523
But before we start talking about Adam(آدم‎), let's look at the story of creation.

152
00:09:43,849 --> 00:09:52,165
Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked this question by a group who came from Yemen,

153
00:09:52,721 --> 00:09:54,499
and this is narrated in Bukhari(بخاری‎).

154
00:09:54,864 --> 00:09:57,050
They came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they said;

155
00:09:57,229 --> 00:10:00,730
يا رسول الله ما أول هذا الأمر؟

156
00:10:01,825 --> 00:10:04,230
"O Rasool Ullah, how did all of this start?"

157
00:10:05,476 --> 00:10:08,216
They wanna know how this all came into existence.

158
00:10:09,422 --> 00:10:11,192
فقال صلى الله عليه وسلم

159
00:10:11,668 --> 00:10:17,834
كَانَ اللَّهُ ولم يكن معه شيء، وفي رواية: ولم يكن قبله شيء،

160
00:10:18,627 --> 00:10:21,818
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "In the beginning, there was Allah,

161
00:10:22,485 --> 00:10:26,638
There was nothing before Him," another narration. "Nothing was with Him."

162
00:10:28,035 --> 00:10:29,956
وكان عرشه على الماء

163
00:10:30,241 --> 00:10:32,262
 "And His throne was on water."

164
00:10:32,952 --> 00:10:35,111
وكتب في الذكر كل شىء،

165
00:10:35,318 --> 00:10:37,556
 "And He wrote in the tablet everything."

166
00:10:37,802 --> 00:10:39,800
وخلق السموات والأرض

167
00:10:40,079 --> 00:10:43,075
 "And He created the heavens and the earth."

168
00:10:44,186 --> 00:10:45,043
Again;

169
00:10:45,964 --> 00:10:51,894
عن عمران بن حصين قال أهل اليمن لرسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

170
00:10:52,227 --> 00:10:57,206
جئناك لنتفقه في الدين ولنسألك عن أول هذا الأمر

171
00:10:57,706 --> 00:11:03,074
فقال كان اللَّه ولم يكن شىء قبله،

172
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:08,896
وكان عرشه على الماء، وكتب في الذكر كل شىء، وخلق السموات والأرض

173
00:11:10,364 --> 00:11:13,607
Narrated by Al-Bukhari(البخاري‎), Imran bin Husain(عمران بن حصين) said;

174
00:11:13,797 --> 00:11:17,131
People from Yemen came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

175
00:11:17,472 --> 00:11:23,769
We have came to you to learn our religion and to ask you, "How did all of this start?"

176
00:11:24,658 --> 00:11:26,214
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

177
00:11:26,412 --> 00:11:31,481
There was Allah and nothing before Him, and His throne was on water,

178
00:11:31,648 --> 00:11:35,949
and He wrote everything in the tablet, and He created the heavens and earth.

179
00:11:37,338 --> 00:11:39,028
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

180
00:11:39,139 --> 00:11:41,774
إن أول ما خلق الله القلم،

181
00:11:41,933 --> 00:11:48,376
 ثم قال له: اكتب، فجرى في تلك الساعة بما هو كائن إلى يوم الساعة

182
00:11:48,885 --> 00:11:53,750
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The first thing Allah created was the Pen,

183
00:11:54,266 --> 00:12:00,620
then Allah ordered it to write so it wrote everything that will happen until the Day of Judgment.

184
00:12:02,056 --> 00:12:03,405
We worry about rizq(رزق),

185
00:12:04,157 --> 00:12:08,072
we worry about our rizq(رزق).

186
00:12:08,241 --> 00:12:11,202
Rizq(رزق) is sustenance, what Allah will provide us.

187
00:12:11,495 --> 00:12:13,503
We worry about our wealth,

188
00:12:14,051 --> 00:12:19,382
we’re always thinking about tomorrow, we are Rizq-o-Phobic.

189
00:12:19,541 --> 00:12:23,517
We have a problem of paranoia of Rizq(رزق).

190
00:12:24,572 --> 00:12:26,282
خلق الإنسان هلوعا

191
00:12:26,669 --> 00:12:30,878
We’re always in a state of despair when it comes to wealth.

192
00:12:31,394 --> 00:12:36,813
We’re always thinking about, “How will we make it in the future?”

193
00:12:37,183 --> 00:12:39,619
worried and terrified and paranoid.

194
00:12:40,611 --> 00:12:41,889
Well listen to this.

195
00:12:42,206 --> 00:12:45,541
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Muslim(ألمسلم).

196
00:12:45,716 --> 00:12:52,486
كتب اللَّه مقادير الخلائق قبل أن يخلق السموات والأرض بخمسين ألف سنة

197
00:12:52,914 --> 00:12:55,757
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Muslim(ألمسلم);

198
00:12:55,964 --> 00:13:03,174
Allah wrote down the sustenance of the creation 50,000 years before He created the heavens and the earth.

199
00:13:04,762 --> 00:13:10,417
Everything that you will get is already written down, not 50,000 years before this day,

200
00:13:10,981 --> 00:13:14,465
but 50,000 years before the heavens and the earth were created.

201
00:13:14,830 --> 00:13:19,621
It's a done deal, what you will get is already written down.

202
00:13:21,065 --> 00:13:23,192
Are you still going to be very concerned about it?

203
00:13:23,930 --> 00:13:25,283
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

204
00:13:25,394 --> 00:13:30,926
خلقت الملائكة من نور وخلق الجان من مارج من نار

205
00:13:31,466 --> 00:13:40,385
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: The angels were created from light and the Jin(جن) were created from fire.

206
00:13:41,608 --> 00:13:45,592
So these are two other creations beside the human being which we know about.

207
00:13:45,656 --> 00:13:51,577
The angels, whom were created from light, and the Jin(جن‎), they were created from fire.

208
00:13:53,092 --> 00:13:55,526
Iblees(إبليس) was from Al-Jinn(الجن),

209
00:13:56,089 --> 00:13:58,999
but because he was so righteous,

210
00:13:59,523 --> 00:14:04,950
he was included with the angels and elevated to a very high level among the angels,

211
00:14:05,632 --> 00:14:07,759
even though he was from Al-Jinn(الجن).

212
00:14:09,363 --> 00:14:13,005
Adam(آدم‎) was created from dirt.

213
00:14:14,083 --> 00:14:15,798
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

214
00:14:17,251 --> 00:14:27,257
وَإِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلَـٰئِكَةِ إِنِّى جَاعِلٌ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً

215
00:14:27,868 --> 00:14:29,566
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

216
00:14:30,654 --> 00:14:33,535
And remember when your Lord said to the angels;

217
00:14:33,638 --> 00:14:38,219
“Verily, I am going to place mankind generations after generations on Earth.”

218
00:14:39,481 --> 00:14:40,989
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

219
00:14:41,362 --> 00:14:44,084
إِنِّى جَاعِلٌ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً

220
00:14:44,815 --> 00:14:49,470
Allah is telling the angels; I will place on Earth a Khalifah(خليفه).

221
00:14:50,343 --> 00:14:51,589
What does “Khalifah(خليفة)” mean?

222
00:14:52,755 --> 00:14:55,260
 “Khalifah(خليفة)” comes from the word “khalaf(خلف)”,

223
00:14:57,038 --> 00:15:04,489
and khalaf(خلف) means to succeed someone else or to assume the position of someone else.

224
00:15:05,648 --> 00:15:07,656
These are the meanings of the word khalaf(خلف).

225
00:15:08,894 --> 00:15:11,071
Allah سبحانه وتعالى, for example, says in Qur’an;

226
00:15:11,508 --> 00:15:18,912
فَخَلَفَ مِنۢ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ أَضَاعُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَٱتَّبَعُوا۟ ٱلشَّهَوَٰتِ ۖ فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا۞

227
00:15:19,125 --> 00:15:27,395
A generation followed them, who lost prayer and followed desires, so they will be misguided.

228
00:15:28,718 --> 00:15:32,409
In this Ayah(آية), it means a generation that came after them,

229
00:15:33,814 --> 00:15:35,841
and that is why we have salaf(سلف‎) and khalaf(خلف).

230
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,080
We say salaf(سلف‎) - who are the salaf(سلف‎)?

231
00:15:38,476 --> 00:15:40,627
The salaf(سلف‎) are the early 3 generations.

232
00:15:40,913 --> 00:15:43,838
Everyone who comes after them, we call them khalaf(خلف).

233
00:15:45,512 --> 00:15:52,085
And then what was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) called when he assumed responsibility after Rasool Allah ﷺ?

234
00:15:52,921 --> 00:15:54,595
خليفة رسول الله

235
00:15:55,524 --> 00:15:56,860
The Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Ullah.

236
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:57,490
Why?

237
00:15:57,627 --> 00:16:01,655
Because he assumed responsibility after Rasool Allah ﷺ

238
00:16:01,758 --> 00:16:03,573
and he came after Rasool Allah ﷺ.

239
00:16:03,597 --> 00:16:08,784
So we see that, in this word, which was used in reference of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), it has two meanings;

240
00:16:09,038 --> 00:16:13,990
first meaning is that he's assuming the responsibility of leading the Ummah(امة) after Rasool Allah ﷺ,

241
00:16:14,387 --> 00:16:20,233
and the second meaning it says that he is coming after Rasool Ullah - Khalifah(خليفة), he comes after.

242
00:16:21,776 --> 00:16:29,058
If we would apply these two meanings to the responsibility or the title that was given to humanity,

243
00:16:29,288 --> 00:16:30,298
Allah سبحانه وتعالى said;

244
00:16:30,338 --> 00:16:32,130
إِنِّى جَاعِلٌ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ خَلِيفَةً

245
00:16:32,273 --> 00:16:34,527
I will place a Khalifah(خليفه) on Earth.

246
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:37,755
So we find two explanations were given;

247
00:16:37,977 --> 00:16:43,796
One explanation says that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has appointed Adam(آدم‎)

248
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:52,095
and his children, his descendants, in the position of responsibility to apply the Laws of Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

249
00:16:53,317 --> 00:16:56,975
so they are representing the Law of Allah سبحانه وتعالى on Earth.

250
00:16:57,047 --> 00:17:02,555
They are given the responsibility of applying the Law of Allah سبحانه وتعالى on Earth

251
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:05,532
and that is the explanation given by Ibn Mas'ud(ابن مسعود).

252
00:17:06,373 --> 00:17:17,650
The second explanation is that humans beings would succeed each other in this world, generation after generation,

253
00:17:18,606 --> 00:17:20,527
and this is the opinion of Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس).

254
00:17:21,273 --> 00:17:26,526
Our responsibility on Earth is to establish Earth according to the Laws of Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

255
00:17:27,385 --> 00:17:30,948
and also we see that we are succeeding each other.

256
00:17:30,988 --> 00:17:35,372
We’re not like the angels who are living, and they’re not marrying and having children.

257
00:17:35,967 --> 00:17:38,657
And we succeed each other on this earth,

258
00:17:39,483 --> 00:17:42,830
that’s why Allah سبحانه وتعالى says about the people of Aad(عاد),

259
00:17:43,041 --> 00:17:47,041
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says that you became the Khalaef(خلائف) of the earth,

260
00:17:47,136 --> 00:17:50,135
which is plural of “Khalifah(خليفة)”, after the people of Nuh(نوح).

261
00:17:51,553 --> 00:17:53,180
So this is the meaning of the word “Khalifah(خليفة)”.

262
00:17:54,118 --> 00:17:59,941
If we look at the Ayah(آية) before this, it would help us in understanding our mission and our role in this world.

263
00:18:00,826 --> 00:18:03,896
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says in the Ayah(آية) right before this Ayah(آية);

264
00:18:04,389 --> 00:18:12,247
هُوَ الَّذي خَلَقَ لَكُم ما فِي الأَرضِ جَميعًا ثُمَّ استَوىٰ إِلَى السَّماءِ

265
00:18:12,493 --> 00:18:23,621
ثُمَّ استَوىٰ إِلَى السَّماءِ فَسَوّاهُنَّ سَبعَ سَماواتٍ ۚ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَيءٍ عَليمٌ۝

266
00:18:24,303 --> 00:18:28,351
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created for you everything in this world.

267
00:18:30,208 --> 00:18:33,242
Everything in this world was created for the human being.

268
00:18:34,425 --> 00:18:37,816
That is the honor that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given this human being,

269
00:18:37,990 --> 00:18:41,213
that everything is created for the exploitation of human beings

270
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:45,334
because they are the ultimate creation of this world

271
00:18:45,596 --> 00:18:51,899
and they are the ones whom Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given the responsibility of establishing this Duniya(دنيا‎), this world.

272
00:18:52,614 --> 00:18:55,566
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created everything for them.

273
00:18:56,804 --> 00:19:02,797
Therefore, we should not give precedence to anything material over the human being.

274
00:19:03,265 --> 00:19:07,035
We should not sacrifice the human being for a material thing

275
00:19:07,416 --> 00:19:12,994
because Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given this noble position to human being

276
00:19:13,185 --> 00:19:17,132
and he made them a Khalifah(خليفة) and he created everything for this human being;

277
00:19:17,259 --> 00:19:18,521
the human being is sacred.

278
00:19:19,298 --> 00:19:22,816
But the way we are dealing with the human being now on the face of the earth

279
00:19:22,981 --> 00:19:27,606
is that we are killing human beings and destroying them for material gain,

280
00:19:29,424 --> 00:19:37,501
and that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ says that the Muslim is sacred in the Eyes of Allah سبحانه وتعالى more than Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

281
00:19:38,850 --> 00:19:41,159
حرمة دم المسلم

282
00:19:41,651 --> 00:19:48,537
 The sanctity and the sacred position that is given to the blood of the Muslim is more than Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

283
00:19:49,513 --> 00:19:52,019
That is the honor that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given to the son of Adam(آدم‎).

284
00:19:52,059 --> 00:19:53,681
وَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِى ءَادَمَ

285
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,419
We have honored the son of Adam(آدَم).

286
00:19:56,975 --> 00:20:01,093
When Allah سبحانه وتعالى told the angels that I will place a Khalifah(خليفه) on Earth,

287
00:20:01,196 --> 00:20:01,967
what did they say?

288
00:20:02,157 --> 00:20:02,811
They said;

289
00:20:02,998 --> 00:20:11,080
قالوا أَتَجعَلُ فيها مَن يُفسِدُ فيها وَيَسفِكُ الدِّماءَ

290
00:20:11,516 --> 00:20:16,468
 وَنَحنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَ

291
00:20:16,714 --> 00:20:22,388
 Will You place therein those who will make mischief therein and shed blood

292
00:20:22,769 --> 00:20:26,359
while we glorify You with praises and thanks?

293
00:20:27,589 --> 00:20:33,247
Are You going to place on Earth someone who will shed blood and cause corruption

294
00:20:33,678 --> 00:20:36,091
when we are glorifying You?

295
00:20:37,583 --> 00:20:42,434
How did the angels know that human beings will corrupt on the face of the earth?

296
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:45,291
Adam(آدم‎) was not placed on the world yet.

297
00:20:45,521 --> 00:20:52,206
Why did the angels say, “You are going to place someone who will cause corruption and shed blood in the world”?

298
00:20:52,873 --> 00:20:55,214
There are two explanations given;

299
00:20:55,603 --> 00:21:01,156
One explanation is that Allah سبحانه وتعالى told the angels ahead of time that

300
00:21:01,608 --> 00:21:03,251
this is what human beings will do;

301
00:21:04,124 --> 00:21:09,574
the second explanation, and this is mentioned by Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس),

302
00:21:10,582 --> 00:21:13,328
that Jin(جن) were living in this world before

303
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:17,256
and they caused corruption and they shed blood

304
00:21:17,565 --> 00:21:21,279
and they fought with each other and they corrupted this world,

305
00:21:21,875 --> 00:21:23,526
and they caused so much evil,

306
00:21:24,692 --> 00:21:34,474
 and then Allah سبحانه وتعالى sent on them armies from the angels, and also Iblees(إبليس), to fight against them,

307
00:21:35,577 --> 00:21:40,268
and then they were pushed and cornered to the islands of the ocean.

308
00:21:41,823 --> 00:21:43,411
So the angels said;

309
00:21:44,141 --> 00:21:48,867
Why are You going to place someone on Earth who would cause corruption and shed blood again?

310
00:21:51,407 --> 00:21:53,203
So these are the two explanations given,

311
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:56,465
there is no Hadith(حديث‎) to support any one of them.

312
00:21:56,592 --> 00:21:59,060
These are two explanations given to the Ayah(آية).

313
00:22:00,155 --> 00:22:01,537
Allah سبحانه وتعالى said;

314
00:22:02,231 --> 00:22:04,319
قالَ إِنّي أَعلَمُ ما لا تَعلَمونَ۞

315
00:22:04,359 --> 00:22:06,731
I know what you know not.

316
00:22:07,604 --> 00:22:10,175
I know what you know not.

317
00:22:10,992 --> 00:22:15,692
Allah سبحانه وتعالى created Adam(آدم‎) and Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

318
00:22:16,223 --> 00:22:22,423
إن اللَّه تعالى خلق آدم من قبضة قبضها من جميع الأرض

319
00:22:22,883 --> 00:22:25,526
فجاء بنو آدم على قدر الأرض

320
00:22:25,796 --> 00:22:29,320
جاء منهم الأحمر والأبيض والأسود وبين ذلك

321
00:22:29,694 --> 00:22:33,313
والسهل والحزن والخبيث والطيب وبين ذلك

322
00:22:34,343 --> 00:22:35,963
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

323
00:22:36,368 --> 00:22:45,803
Allah created Adam(آدَم) from a handful of dirt, picked from all of the Earth,

324
00:22:46,679 --> 00:22:52,477
so the children of Adam(آدَم) became red, white and black, and everything in between,

325
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:58,360
and they became soft and tough, bad and good, and everything in between.

326
00:22:59,253 --> 00:23:00,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

327
00:23:01,068 --> 00:23:05,524
Allah سبحانه وتعالى created Adam(آدم‎) from a handful of dirt.

328
00:23:06,437 --> 00:23:11,576
This dirt was taken from different parts of the earth.

329
00:23:12,013 --> 00:23:17,561
So there was black soil, there was white soil, there was yellow soil, different colors.

330
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:24,996
And then some of this soil was taken from mountains, and some of it was taken from valleys, and it was mixed together.

331
00:23:26,474 --> 00:23:32,292
So the son of Adam(آدم‎), the descendants of Adam(آدم‎), came out in different colors

332
00:23:32,739 --> 00:23:36,211
because the dirt they were created from is from different colors,

333
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:39,233
and they came out with different qualities

334
00:23:39,948 --> 00:23:43,777
because some of this dirt was taken from mountains, and some of it was valleys,

335
00:23:44,055 --> 00:23:48,893
some of it was from fertile land, and some of it was from infertile land.

336
00:23:49,416 --> 00:23:52,146
So you have some of them are righteous and some of them are evil,

337
00:23:52,343 --> 00:23:55,140
some of them are easy to deal with and some of them are tough.

338
00:23:55,805 --> 00:23:58,572
They came out according to the material they were created from.

339
00:23:59,753 --> 00:24:01,528
What was Adam(آدم‎) created from?

340
00:24:01,697 --> 00:24:02,675
Turab(تراب‎),

341
00:24:03,433 --> 00:24:04,023
dirt.

342
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:10,014
But that was not the only name that was given to the material we were created from.

343
00:24:10,739 --> 00:24:19,815
We find in Qur’an that the components of our body were described with different terms.

344
00:24:21,243 --> 00:24:24,240
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has called it Turab(تراب‎),

345
00:24:25,069 --> 00:24:26,180
which means dirt;

346
00:24:27,271 --> 00:24:30,178
Allah has called it Tin(طين),

347
00:24:30,525 --> 00:24:31,785
which means clay;

348
00:24:32,648 --> 00:24:35,214
Tinin Laazib(طين لازب), sticky clay;

349
00:24:35,924 --> 00:24:36,995
Salsal(صلصال),

350
00:24:37,154 --> 00:24:38,503
 sounding clay;

351
00:24:38,999 --> 00:24:40,398
Hama’im Masnoon(حمإ مسنون),

352
00:24:40,706 --> 00:24:42,233
black smooth mud.

353
00:24:43,662 --> 00:24:48,602
Why were these different terms used to refer to the material we were created from?

354
00:24:50,031 --> 00:24:51,003
Turab(تراب‎),

355
00:24:51,331 --> 00:24:52,055
tin(طين),

356
00:24:52,352 --> 00:24:53,444
Salsal(صلصال),

357
00:24:53,751 --> 00:24:54,991
Hama’im masnoon(حمإ مسنون),

358
00:24:55,269 --> 00:24:56,389
Tinin Laazib(طين لازب)

359
00:24:56,859 --> 00:24:57,691
 dirt,

360
00:24:58,099 --> 00:24:58,843
mud,

361
00:24:59,141 --> 00:25:00,113
clay,

362
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:01,779
sounding clay,

363
00:25:01,978 --> 00:25:03,654
black smooth mud.

364
00:25:05,073 --> 00:25:07,447
In the beginning, it was dirt.

365
00:25:08,012 --> 00:25:08,806
turab(تراب‎)

366
00:25:09,292 --> 00:25:12,338
dirt, soil that was taken from the earth,

367
00:25:13,677 --> 00:25:14,915
and that is turab(تراب‎).

368
00:25:16,296 --> 00:25:26,821
And then this dirt was mixed with the basis of every living being, and that is water.

369
00:25:27,665 --> 00:25:29,750
وَجَعَلنا مِنَ الماءِ كُلَّ شَيءٍ حَيٍّ ۖ

370
00:25:29,969 --> 00:25:32,836
We created from water every living being.

371
00:25:34,086 --> 00:25:38,678
When it was mixed with water, it became mud, tin(طين).

372
00:25:39,724 --> 00:25:42,836
And then this mud was left for a while,

373
00:25:43,315 --> 00:25:52,114
and when you leave mud for a while and the moisture in it reduces, it becomes sticky.

374
00:25:52,420 --> 00:25:55,143
In the beginning, it is loose mud because it has a lot of water,

375
00:25:55,282 --> 00:25:58,357
then when the water level decreases and the moisture decreases,

376
00:25:58,536 --> 00:26:00,202
it becomes sticky

377
00:26:00,450 --> 00:26:03,419
and it holds to your hands; sticky,

378
00:26:04,084 --> 00:26:07,239
and that is Tin Laazib(طين لازب), sticky clay.

379
00:26:07,764 --> 00:26:13,073
And then that sticky clay was left for a longer while,

380
00:26:13,688 --> 00:26:18,281
the smell of it changed and the color of it became darker,

381
00:26:18,896 --> 00:26:22,081
and that is Hama’im Masnoon(حمإ مسنون),

382
00:26:23,486 --> 00:26:28,232
which is black, smooth, and smelly clay

383
00:26:28,663 --> 00:26:30,623
because it was left there for a while.

384
00:26:31,060 --> 00:26:40,637
That material was taken, and Allah سبحانه وتعالى molded out of it the form of Adam(آدم‎), the body of Adam(آدم‎).

385
00:26:42,373 --> 00:26:50,634
That body was left to dry, and it turned into Salsal Kal-Fakhar(صلصال كَٱلفخار)

386
00:26:51,849 --> 00:26:54,378
clay-like pottery.

387
00:26:55,232 --> 00:27:00,719
When you knock on dry clay, pottery, what happens?

388
00:27:01,185 --> 00:27:02,821
It makes a ringing sound,

389
00:27:03,357 --> 00:27:07,936
and that is Salsal(صلصال), Min Salsalah(من صلصلة), it makes a ringing sound like a bell.

390
00:27:09,226 --> 00:27:15,763
So the body, the form of Adam(آدم‎), the empty form of Adam(آدم‎) that did not have the soul yet, it was just a material.

391
00:27:16,378 --> 00:27:20,851
It was left to dry, and then when you would knock on it, it would make this ringing sound.

392
00:27:21,020 --> 00:27:31,443
It is said, this is not a Hadith(حديث), but it is said that Iblis(إبليس), he saw this body lying on the ground.

393
00:27:31,949 --> 00:27:33,467
He didn’t know what it was,

394
00:27:34,717 --> 00:27:39,885
so Iblis(إبليس) walked up to the body of Adam(آدم‎) and he knocked it,

395
00:27:40,415 --> 00:27:45,266
and it made a ringing sound and it was hollow.

396
00:27:46,238 --> 00:27:49,234
When he knocked it, he knew that it was hollow from the inside, empty.

397
00:27:49,968 --> 00:27:50,514
He said;

398
00:27:50,613 --> 00:27:52,399
هذا خلق لا يتمالك

399
00:27:52,766 --> 00:27:54,988
When he found out that it’s hollow, he said;

400
00:27:55,087 --> 00:27:57,647
This is a creation that is weak.

401
00:27:58,430 --> 00:27:59,659
It’s hollow from the inside.

402
00:28:00,989 --> 00:28:02,010
And then he said;

403
00:28:02,407 --> 00:28:09,699
لن يسلط عليك لهينك ولا أن يسلط علي لا عصيانك

404
00:28:09,967 --> 00:28:15,005
If I am given influence over you, I will guide you astray

405
00:28:15,917 --> 00:28:20,253
and if you are given influence over me, I would disobey you.

406
00:28:21,592 --> 00:28:23,866
He is our enemy from day one.

407
00:28:24,419 --> 00:28:27,788
Adam(آدَم) is not even alive yet,

408
00:28:28,255 --> 00:28:31,905
it's just a body that is lying there, and he said;

409
00:28:31,945 --> 00:28:34,802
If you are given influence over me, I'm going to disobey you.

410
00:28:35,169 --> 00:28:37,094
Let's do the same thing and disobey him.

411
00:28:38,066 --> 00:28:41,280
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Muslim(ألمسلم);

412
00:28:42,391 --> 00:28:45,943
خلق الله آدم على صورته

413
00:28:47,238 --> 00:28:50,878
In the beginning, we know that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created Adam(آدَم) with His own Hands.

414
00:28:51,662 --> 00:28:55,971
Adam(آدَم) was honored that he was created with the Hands of Allah سبحانه وتعالى,

415
00:28:56,387 --> 00:28:59,780
a great honor and that is mentioned in the Hadith(حديث) of Al-shafa'ah(الشفاعة‎)

416
00:28:59,959 --> 00:29:03,883
when the humans would go to Sayyiduna Adam(سيدنا آدم‎) on the Day of Judgment, and they would say;

417
00:29:03,982 --> 00:29:07,286
You are the one whom Allah سبحانه وتعالى blew his soul into you

418
00:29:07,326 --> 00:29:10,550
and you are the one whom Allah سبحانه وتعالى created with His own Hands

419
00:29:10,689 --> 00:29:15,394
and you are the one whom Allah سبحانه وتعالى made the angels bow down to, to make Sujud(سجود).

420
00:29:16,931 --> 00:29:22,537
Honoring that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given to Adam(آدم‎), he was created with the Hands of Allah.

421
00:29:23,598 --> 00:29:26,703
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by Muslim(ألمسلم);

422
00:29:27,824 --> 00:29:30,741
خلق الله آدم على صورته

423
00:29:31,138 --> 00:29:34,531
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created Adam(آدَم) on his image.

424
00:29:35,994 --> 00:29:37,561
On his image.

425
00:29:38,225 --> 00:29:42,818
Al-Nawawi(النووي‎) gives an explanation to this Hadith(حديث).

426
00:29:43,680 --> 00:29:44,879
He says;

427
00:29:45,951 --> 00:29:50,925
What is meant by, Allah has created Adam(آدَم) on his image?

428
00:29:51,679 --> 00:29:56,570
It is not talking about the Image of Allah, it is talking about the image of Adam(آدَم).

429
00:29:58,157 --> 00:30:02,791
Allah created Adam(آدَم) on the image of Adam(آدَم).

430
00:30:03,813 --> 00:30:05,956
You might wonder, What does that mean?

431
00:30:06,492 --> 00:30:09,795
What do you mean Allah created Adam(آدَم) on Adam's image?

432
00:30:10,599 --> 00:30:19,057
That would mean that Allah سبحانه وتعالى created Adam(آدَم) as he was in his adult form that remained with him.

433
00:30:20,039 --> 00:30:24,460
In other words, Adam(آدَم) did not go through the stages that we go through;

434
00:30:24,732 --> 00:30:32,015
of being an embryo, and then a fetus, and then an infant, and then a child, and then an adult.

435
00:30:33,345 --> 00:30:34,794
خلق الله آدم على صورته

436
00:30:34,834 --> 00:30:36,544
Adam(آدم‎) was created on his image,

437
00:30:36,718 --> 00:30:39,996
he didn't go through changes of images like we do.

438
00:30:40,244 --> 00:30:43,438
We go through different changes of images;

439
00:30:43,657 --> 00:30:46,979
from embryo to fetus…

440
00:30:47,089 --> 00:30:50,863
it looks very different when you go from the one cell to another…

441
00:30:51,111 --> 00:30:55,597
then it multiplies, and the embryo is in the early stages, and then the fetus.

442
00:30:55,823 --> 00:30:59,127
If you look at it, the image could change within days.

443
00:31:00,298 --> 00:31:04,415
But with Adam(آدم‎), he was created on that image from day One,

444
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:10,372
and this is diametrically opposed to what the Theory of Evolution says.

445
00:31:11,821 --> 00:31:18,151
The Theory of Evolution states that human beings came through an evolution process

446
00:31:18,935 --> 00:31:21,346
that started with a chemical reaction

447
00:31:21,822 --> 00:31:25,879
and then the one cell, the single cell, and then multiple cells,

448
00:31:26,078 --> 00:31:31,321
and then it goes up and up and up until it reaches to the human being in the end of that long chain.

449
00:31:31,838 --> 00:31:36,064
That is contradicting, completely contradicting, to the truth

450
00:31:36,481 --> 00:31:42,408
because Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created Adam(آدم‎) with His own Hands on that image

451
00:31:42,835 --> 00:31:44,938
that remained with Adam(آدم‎) until he died.

452
00:31:45,821 --> 00:31:51,202
But let me say that Islam does not completely disapprove everything in the Theory of Evolution;

453
00:31:51,519 --> 00:31:54,307
Islam disapproves some and approves some.

454
00:31:54,823 --> 00:32:05,414
Islam disapproves the part of the Theory of Evolution that states that nature is the creator or that things came out of random.

455
00:32:06,674 --> 00:32:15,632
Islam is against the part of the Theory of Evolution that states that human being evolved from a single cell

456
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:23,458
and then it went up to the ape, which they call the closest relative of the human being, and then the human being.

457
00:32:23,864 --> 00:32:30,889
But Islam is not opposed to the part of the Theory of Evolution that says that species adapt to their environment.

458
00:32:31,524 --> 00:32:37,635
We see that around us, that different species learn how to adapt to different environments.

459
00:32:37,963 --> 00:32:40,713
But, we say that that happens with the Will of Allah.

460
00:32:41,536 --> 00:32:46,159
Allahسبحانه وتعالى blew the soul into Adam(آدم‎).

461
00:32:47,102 --> 00:32:48,064
Ar-Ruh(الروح).

462
00:32:48,867 --> 00:32:54,959
Our body without Ar-Ruh(الروح) is part of the earth, it is dirt.

463
00:32:55,871 --> 00:33:05,961
Our body is made up of carbon, oxygen, copper, iron, sulfur that is our body.

464
00:33:07,002 --> 00:33:11,886
And when the soul leaves, our body decomposes into its origin.

465
00:33:13,196 --> 00:33:14,426
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

466
00:33:14,506 --> 00:33:20,894
مِنْهَا خَلَقْنَـٰكُمْ وَفِيهَا نُعِيدُكُمْ وَمِنْهَا نُخْرِجُكُمْ تَارَةً أُخْرَىٰ

467
00:33:21,083 --> 00:33:26,260
We created you from Earth, and you will return to Earth, and then We will resurrect you again from Earth.

468
00:33:26,994 --> 00:33:28,810
We are nothing without the soul.

469
00:33:29,504 --> 00:33:33,148
The essence of life is not in this materialistic body,

470
00:33:33,541 --> 00:33:42,202
this body that we have is dead, it is material components that are dirt, it came from the dirt, from the earth.

471
00:33:43,253 --> 00:33:47,386
What puts life in us is the soul, and that is the secret of life

472
00:33:47,544 --> 00:33:52,336
and it remains as a secret even with all of the advancement in science and technology that we have.

473
00:33:53,636 --> 00:33:57,138
They came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: Tell us about the soul.

474
00:33:57,366 --> 00:33:58,344
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

475
00:33:58,384 --> 00:34:03,711
وَيَسْـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلرُّوحِ ۖ قُلِ ٱلرُّوحُ مِنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّى وَمَآ أُوتِيتُم مِّنَ ٱلْعِلْمِ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا۝

476
00:34:03,820 --> 00:34:09,585
They ask you about the soul. Tell them that the knowledge of the soul belongs to Allah,

477
00:34:09,675 --> 00:34:11,996
and you have been given very limited knowledge.

478
00:34:13,574 --> 00:34:16,208
The soul is a secret that only Allah knows,

479
00:34:16,635 --> 00:34:18,877
and our knowledge of the soul is very limited.

480
00:34:19,016 --> 00:34:22,647
This question was asked to Rasool Allah ﷺ fourteen hundred years ago;

481
00:34:22,845 --> 00:34:25,533
our knowledge about the soul did not change much since then.

482
00:34:27,577 --> 00:34:28,833
We don’t know much about the soul.

483
00:34:29,044 --> 00:34:35,605
The Soviet Union, under communism, they disbelieved in anything metaphysical.

484
00:34:36,706 --> 00:34:42,698
They only believed in the physical world; everything that is metaphysical, they didn't believe in it.

485
00:34:43,630 --> 00:34:46,309
So they thought that they could create a human being,

486
00:34:47,509 --> 00:34:52,609
so in their labs, they looked at the composition of the human body

487
00:34:52,649 --> 00:34:59,530
and they found out that it’s made of copper, and sulfur, and iron, and carbon, and oxygen, and hydrogen.

488
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:05,784
They brought those elements and they mixed them together with the same ratio that exists in our body,

489
00:35:06,323 --> 00:35:10,793
and then they kept on sending some electrical shocks on it thinking that that would give it life.

490
00:35:12,293 --> 00:35:17,753
It is not our body that makes us alive, our body is dirt, it belongs to this earth.

491
00:35:18,356 --> 00:35:24,658
What makes us alive is the secret which Allah سبحانه وتعالى has placed in us, and that is the soul, Ar-Ruh(الروح).

492
00:35:25,253 --> 00:35:27,066
 And that is something we don’t know about.

493
00:35:28,042 --> 00:35:31,510
That is the difference between life and death, Ar-Ruh(الروح).

494
00:35:32,090 --> 00:35:36,071
That is why when Musa(موسی) and the magicians were competing,

495
00:35:36,896 --> 00:35:39,643
the magicians were throwing their sticks

496
00:35:39,723 --> 00:35:44,841
and they were making those sticks look like snakes through optical illusion,

497
00:35:45,444 --> 00:35:51,155
but with Musa(موسی), his stick turned into an actual living snake

498
00:35:51,464 --> 00:35:54,274
because Allah سبحانه وتعالى’s the One, Who controls life,

499
00:35:54,631 --> 00:35:58,352
so Allah put life in that stick and it became a snake.

500
00:35:59,186 --> 00:36:04,910
But with the magicians, all what they could do is fool the people through an optical illusion

501
00:36:05,185 --> 00:36:07,510
because they do not have the power to put life,

502
00:36:08,113 --> 00:36:14,114
and when they saw what was happening with the stick of Musa(موسی), they knew that this is a miracle

503
00:36:14,257 --> 00:36:15,937
and they immediately became Muslim

504
00:36:16,136 --> 00:36:21,295
because they knew that this is something outside the capacity and the capability of the human being.

505
00:36:21,747 --> 00:36:26,361
So the soul is what gives us life, and this is as Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

506
00:36:26,401 --> 00:36:27,334
مِنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّى

507
00:36:27,374 --> 00:36:31,343
This is knowledge that belongs to Allah, this is an issue that belongs to Allah.

508
00:36:32,113 --> 00:36:36,795
When the soul entered into the body of Adam(آدم‎), the first thing that happened is,

509
00:36:37,556 --> 00:36:38,668
 he sneezed.

510
00:36:39,787 --> 00:36:44,082
When the soul entered into his body, Adam(آدم‎) sneezed.

511
00:36:44,765 --> 00:36:49,550
لما خلق اللَّه آدم ونفخ فيه الروح عطس

512
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:56,899
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says when Allah سبحانه وتعالى created Adam(آدم‎) and He blew the soul into him,

513
00:36:57,114 --> 00:36:58,704
Adam(آدم‎) sneezed.

514
00:37:00,136 --> 00:37:02,176
فقال الحمد للَّه

515
00:37:02,533 --> 00:37:04,771
Adam(آدم‎) said: Al-hamdulillah(ألحمدلله).

516
00:37:04,850 --> 00:37:06,826
 “Praise be to Allah.”

517
00:37:07,776 --> 00:37:09,165
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told him;

518
00:37:09,205 --> 00:37:10,498
يرحمك اللَّه

519
00:37:11,760 --> 00:37:14,514
 “The Mercy of Allah be upon you.”

520
00:37:15,690 --> 00:37:22,666
The first thing that happened to Adam(آدم‎) was the deliverance of mercy onto him from Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

521
00:37:23,523 --> 00:37:28,304
When he was created, Allah سبحانه وتعالى Himself told Adam(آدم‎);

522
00:37:28,344 --> 00:37:29,402
يرحمك اللَّه

523
00:37:29,759 --> 00:37:31,415
The Mercy of Allah be upon you.

524
00:37:31,559 --> 00:37:34,682
That was the first thing that was told to Sayyiduna Adam عليه السلام.

525
00:37:34,928 --> 00:37:37,333
He had the Mercy of Allah سبحانه وتعالى from the beginning.

526
00:37:37,936 --> 00:37:39,294
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told him;

527
00:37:39,334 --> 00:37:43,270
اذهب إلى أولئك الملائكة إلى نفر منهم جلوس

528
00:37:44,238 --> 00:37:48,667
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told Adam(آدم‎): “Go to those angels who are sitting over there.”

529
00:37:48,849 --> 00:37:55,820
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told Adam(آدم‎) to go to those angels and to deliver Salam(سلام‎) to them.

530
00:37:56,169 --> 00:38:02,784
اذهب إلى أولئك الملائكة إلى نفر منهم جلوس فقل السلام عليكم

531
00:38:03,419 --> 00:38:07,760
 “Go to those angels who are sitting over there and tell them;

532
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:09,165
السلام عليكم

533
00:38:10,038 --> 00:38:12,530
Allah سبحانه وتعالى is teaching Adam(آدم‎),

534
00:38:13,014 --> 00:38:14,937
“Go to those angels and tell them;

535
00:38:14,977 --> 00:38:15,863
السلام عليكم

536
00:38:16,648 --> 00:38:18,554
Adam(آدم‎) went up to the angels and he said;

537
00:38:18,594 --> 00:38:19,985
السلام عليكم‏!‏

538
00:38:20,265 --> 00:38:24,129
قالوا وعليك السلام ورحمة اللَّه

539
00:38:25,042 --> 00:38:26,828
He went to the angels, he told them;

540
00:38:26,899 --> 00:38:27,718
السلام عليكم

541
00:38:27,758 --> 00:38:28,352
They said;

542
00:38:28,590 --> 00:38:32,714
وعليك السلام ورحمة اللَّه وبركاته

543
00:38:33,151 --> 00:38:39,587
 “May the Peace of Allah سبحانه وتعالى be upon you and His Mercy be upon you and His Blessings be upon you.”

544
00:38:40,612 --> 00:38:44,147
 So Adam(آدم‎) came back to Allah سبحانه وتعالى, Allah told him;

545
00:38:44,258 --> 00:38:48,766
إن هذه تحيتك وتحية بنيك بينهم

546
00:38:48,972 --> 00:38:52,404
“This is your greeting and this is the greeting of your descendents.”

547
00:38:52,650 --> 00:38:56,961
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى has taught us our greeting from the beginning

548
00:38:57,001 --> 00:39:03,795
and it was taught to Adam عليه السلام, and this is the greeting that Allah سبحانه وتعالى wanted for the children of Adam(آدم‎).

549
00:39:03,842 --> 00:39:05,215
It is; Assalam O Alaikum(السلام عليكم).

550
00:39:05,525 --> 00:39:07,291
“Peace be upon you.

551
00:39:07,938 --> 00:39:13,019
” Not “hi”, “hello”, “good morning”, or “good night”, or “what's up”.

552
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,954
السلام عليكم

553
00:39:16,058 --> 00:39:19,570
 Peace be upon you, first,

554
00:39:20,277 --> 00:39:24,054
and then after that, after you deliver the peace…

555
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:28,782
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) look at the beauty of Islam, we are spreading peace.

556
00:39:28,822 --> 00:39:30,607
أفشوا السلام بينكم

557
00:39:30,813 --> 00:39:33,948
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: “Spread peace among you.”

558
00:39:34,393 --> 00:39:36,534
Spread peace whenever you see somebody,

559
00:39:36,709 --> 00:39:37,756
السلام عليكم

560
00:39:37,812 --> 00:39:39,375
“Peace be upon you.”

561
00:39:39,494 --> 00:39:41,455
Alhamdulillah (الحمد لله) on the Niʿmah(نعمة) of being Muslim.

562
00:39:42,193 --> 00:39:43,066
After you say;

563
00:39:43,106 --> 00:39:44,135
السلام عليكم

564
00:39:44,375 --> 00:39:48,180
And you receive the blessing of your brother telling you;

565
00:39:48,220 --> 00:39:50,599
وعليكم السلام ورحمة الله وبركاته

566
00:39:50,734 --> 00:39:53,598
Then you are free to use any greeting you want,

567
00:39:53,878 --> 00:40:05,668
whether it is “hi” or “hello” or “good morning” or “good afternoon” or “storestee” or “صح خبس”, or “cómo estás”...or whatever, whatever you want…

568
00:40:06,017 --> 00:40:07,168
”Sabah al-khayr(صباح الخير)”.

569
00:40:07,208 --> 00:40:08,525
In the beginning, Assalam O Alaikum(السلام عليكم).

570
00:40:08,565 --> 00:40:11,037
And then after that you could use any greeting you want

571
00:40:11,077 --> 00:40:14,625
because we know that Rasool Allah ﷺ used to tell the Sahabah(صحابة) for example: Kaifa Asbahat(كيف أصبحت)”.

572
00:40:15,299 --> 00:40:17,334
“Kaifa Asbaht(كيف أصبحت)” is like saying “good morning”.

573
00:40:17,857 --> 00:40:19,274
But in the beginning, it needs to be:

574
00:40:19,322 --> 00:40:20,500
السلام عليكم

575
00:40:21,167 --> 00:40:23,127
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

576
00:40:23,508 --> 00:40:30,363
وَإِذْ أَخَذَ رَبُّكَ مِنۢ بَنِىٓ ءَادَمَ مِن ظُهُورِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ

577
00:40:30,514 --> 00:40:36,352
وَأَشْهَدَهُمْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ أَلَسْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ ۖ

578
00:40:36,526 --> 00:40:41,876
قَالُوا۟ بَلَىٰ ۛ شَهِدْنَآ ۛ أَن تَقُولُوا۟ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَـٰمَةِ

579
00:40:41,992 --> 00:40:49,098
أَن تَقُولُوا۟ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَـٰمَةِ إِنَّا كُنَّا عَنْ هَـٰذَا غَـٰفِلِينَ ۝

580
00:40:49,329 --> 00:40:59,585
أَوْ تَقُولُوٓا۟ إِنَّمَآ أَشْرَكَ ءَابَآؤُنَا مِن قَبْلُ وَكُنَّا ذُرِّيَّةً مِّنۢ بَعْدِهِمْ ۖ

581
00:40:59,815 --> 00:41:03,720
أَفَتُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ ٱلْمُبْطِلُونَ۝

582
00:41:04,109 --> 00:41:05,618
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

583
00:41:06,096 --> 00:41:12,970
And remember when your Lord brought forth from the children of Adam(آدَم) from their loins their seed

584
00:41:14,187 --> 00:41:19,300
and made them testify as to themselves, saying: “Am I not your Lord?”

585
00:41:19,427 --> 00:41:21,244
They said: “Yes, we testify.”

586
00:41:21,673 --> 00:41:25,746
Lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection: “Verily, we have been unaware of this.”

587
00:41:27,024 --> 00:41:31,161
This is talking about a very important concept, and that is Al-Mithaq(الميثاق), the covenant.

588
00:41:32,971 --> 00:41:36,915
Do you know that there is an agreement between us and Allah سبحانه وتعالى?

589
00:41:38,755 --> 00:41:42,743
Do you know that there is a covenant between us and Allah, an agreement?

590
00:41:43,525 --> 00:41:45,796
This Ayah(آية‎) is talking about that agreement.

591
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:54,511
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has made a covenant with us and that is we worship no one but Him,

592
00:41:56,031 --> 00:42:01,450
and we witnessed upon ourselves that we shall not worship anyone but Allah.

593
00:42:02,767 --> 00:42:04,418
And then Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

594
00:42:04,672 --> 00:42:07,804
Lest you should say on the Day of Judgment that “we are unaware of this.”

595
00:42:07,982 --> 00:42:11,768
Don't say, in other words, don’t say on the Day of Judgement that “I didn't know about that.”

596
00:42:12,213 --> 00:42:13,911
We have given this covenant.

597
00:42:15,118 --> 00:42:17,829
Two explanations have been given to this Ayah(آية).

598
00:42:19,662 --> 00:42:26,732
One explanation says that this covenant is a covenant of Fitrah(فطرة‎).

599
00:42:27,462 --> 00:42:29,177
Fitrah(فطرة‎) is the original state;

600
00:42:29,883 --> 00:42:36,111
everyone of us has an original state, and that original state is Islam, Al-Fitrah(الفطرة‎).

601
00:42:36,920 --> 00:42:39,738
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has created us on fitrah(فطرة‎).

602
00:42:40,738 --> 00:42:45,857
Rasool Allah ﷺ says everyone is born on the fitrah(فطرة‎) of Islam, on the original creation of Islam,

603
00:42:45,976 --> 00:42:49,759
and then their parents make them a Christian or a Jew or a Zoroastrian.

604
00:42:50,465 --> 00:42:51,926
But in the beginning, we are Muslim.

605
00:42:52,172 --> 00:42:59,026
Every one of us is Muslim and that’s why many who embrace Islam - they don’t like to be called “converts”;

606
00:43:00,470 --> 00:43:04,034
they say: “We never converted to Islam, we reverted.

607
00:43:04,709 --> 00:43:06,087
We reverted to Islam

608
00:43:06,357 --> 00:43:11,929
because we were Muslim in the beginning and then we lost it and then we came back to it again.

609
00:43:12,361 --> 00:43:18,937
So we are reverts because everyone of us started out as a Muslim submitting to Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

610
00:43:21,070 --> 00:43:23,673
The next explanation is that

611
00:43:24,260 --> 00:43:32,672
Allah سبحانه وتعالى took out the seed of Adam(آدم‎), every one of us, from Adam(آدم‎) until the Day of Judgment,

612
00:43:32,856 --> 00:43:33,892
 every one of us,

613
00:43:34,551 --> 00:43:37,075
and we were placed in the Hand of Allah سبحانه وتعالى

614
00:43:38,321 --> 00:43:40,638
and then Allah سبحانه وتعالى asked us;

615
00:43:41,534 --> 00:43:43,010
Am I your Lord?

616
00:43:43,748 --> 00:43:44,903
And we said: “Yes.”

617
00:43:45,343 --> 00:43:47,424
And that is mentioned in a hadith(حديث‎).

618
00:43:48,130 --> 00:43:52,162
Now the only reason why we have another opinion is that

619
00:43:52,248 --> 00:43:56,102
is because some of the Ulema(علماء‎) critiqued this hadith(حديث‎).

620
00:43:56,515 --> 00:43:59,134
Some of them accept it as strong and some don't.

621
00:43:59,571 --> 00:44:00,419
But the hadith(حديث‎) is;

622
00:44:00,459 --> 00:44:07,816
إن الله أخذ الميثاق من ظهر آدم  بنعمان - يوم عرفة - وأخرج من صلبه

623
00:44:07,879 --> 00:44:12,234
 كل ذرية ذرأها، فنثرهم بين يديه كالذر،

624
00:44:12,416 --> 00:44:16,360
ثم كلمهم قبله، قال: أَلَسْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ ۖ قَالُوا۟ بَلَىٰ

625
00:44:17,924 --> 00:44:21,999
Allah has taken the covenant in Nuʿman(نعمان) - the Day of ʿArafah(عرفة).

626
00:44:22,396 --> 00:44:27,813
Allah has taken out of Adam(آدَم) all of his seed and scattered them in His Hand like pearls,

627
00:44:28,329 --> 00:44:29,733
then Allah asked them;

628
00:44:29,956 --> 00:44:32,044
Isn’t it that I am your Lord?

629
00:44:32,145 --> 00:44:33,534
They said: Yes.

630
00:44:33,867 --> 00:44:38,243
According to this hadith(حديث‎), every one of us has spoken to Allah سبحانه وتعالى and said;

631
00:44:38,291 --> 00:44:42,037
Yes, You are our Lord and we will worship nobody but You.

632
00:44:43,870 --> 00:44:45,270
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

633
00:44:45,532 --> 00:44:54,512
وَعَلَّمَ ءَادَمَ ٱلْأَسْمَاءَ كُلَّهَا ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى ٱلْمَلَـٰئِكَةِ

634
00:44:54,726 --> 00:44:59,091
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says: And He taught Adam(آدَم) all of the names.

635
00:45:00,290 --> 00:45:05,856
In tafsir(تفسير‎), it mentions, this is the opinion of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه,

636
00:45:07,134 --> 00:45:09,799
that Allah سبحانه وتعالى taught him the names of everything

637
00:45:11,315 --> 00:45:16,053
the nouns and the verbs and the adjectives, all the names.

638
00:45:16,203 --> 00:45:20,291
And if we take this literally, it would mean that he knew the names of everything.

639
00:45:21,918 --> 00:45:25,251
But then there is another meaning that is mentioned also,

640
00:45:26,949 --> 00:45:33,159
and that is that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given him the ability to identify objects

641
00:45:33,842 --> 00:45:36,651
and to designate names for these objects,

642
00:45:37,913 --> 00:45:40,627
and that is the ability of speaking a language.

643
00:45:42,133 --> 00:45:48,177
Again, it’s the ability to identify objects and to designate names for these objects,

644
00:45:48,257 --> 00:45:51,167
and we find that that is a human ability.

645
00:45:52,811 --> 00:45:55,048
We have different languages in the world,

646
00:45:55,710 --> 00:46:01,313
and all of these languages were founded by human beings by giving names to objects

647
00:46:01,607 --> 00:46:05,402
and then finding verbs and adjectives to tie these things together.

648
00:46:06,449 --> 00:46:10,368
Now imagine that we did not have this ability;

649
00:46:11,177 --> 00:46:15,010
so you want to tell your friend about a tree,

650
00:46:15,859 --> 00:46:18,204
you cannot name and identify that object

651
00:46:18,244 --> 00:46:20,759
so what you have to do is take him to the tree,

652
00:46:21,132 --> 00:46:22,958
or you want to tell him about an apple

653
00:46:23,196 --> 00:46:27,284
you cannot describe the apple, you have to bring an apple to him and start pointing at it.

654
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:33,842
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given the son of Adam(آدم‎) this ability, and Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

655
00:46:34,287 --> 00:46:37,236
 خَلَقَ ٱلْإِنسَـٰنَ ۝ عَلَّمَهُ ٱلْبَيَانَ۝

656
00:46:37,276 --> 00:46:42,253
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى created the human and He taught him bayan(بيان), the ability of speaking, speech.

657
00:46:43,451 --> 00:46:46,316
This is an ability that Allah سبحانه وتعالى did not give the angels.

658
00:46:46,396 --> 00:46:51,407
The angels only know specific knowledge which Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given them

659
00:46:51,741 --> 00:46:53,820
because they do not need this knowledge.

660
00:46:53,860 --> 00:46:56,225
Allah سبحانه وتعالى taught them what they need.

661
00:46:56,820 --> 00:47:00,781
They get orders, they receive orders from Allah سبحانه وتعالى and they do what they’re commanded.

662
00:47:00,923 --> 00:47:02,261
يفعلون ما يؤمرون

663
00:47:02,844 --> 00:47:08,108
But because the human being - Allah سبحانه وتعالى created him for the Khilafah(خلافة‎) on Earth.

664
00:47:08,369 --> 00:47:09,854
عن عمارة الأرض

665
00:47:10,655 --> 00:47:17,091
“To the establishment of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) on Earth,” and to establish this earth and live in it.

666
00:47:17,694 --> 00:47:19,805
That ability is necessary for us.

667
00:47:19,948 --> 00:47:22,440
Imagine how our life would be;

668
00:47:22,526 --> 00:47:26,923
actually, we wouldn't be living if we didn't have the ability to identify objects and name them.

669
00:47:27,169 --> 00:47:29,962
This is a necessity for us to communicate,

670
00:47:30,295 --> 00:47:33,491
and Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given the son of Adam(آدم‎) that ability.

671
00:47:34,753 --> 00:47:35,899
So we’re able to name things,

672
00:47:35,939 --> 00:47:39,955
and you find out that we’re producing every now and then thousands and thousands of objects

673
00:47:40,137 --> 00:47:43,338
and we’re designating names to these objects,

674
00:47:44,179 --> 00:47:47,743
microphone, speakers - all of these are new names,

675
00:47:48,052 --> 00:47:53,924
but the son of Adam(آدم‎) is able and throw a thousand things in the market, we have the ability to find names for them.

676
00:47:55,868 --> 00:47:57,543
وَعَلَّمَ ءَادَمَ ٱلْأَسْمَاءَ كُلَّهَا

677
00:47:57,773 --> 00:48:00,238
Allah سبحانه وتعالى taught Adam (آدم‎) all of the names.

678
00:48:01,142 --> 00:48:03,127
ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى ٱلْمَلَـٰئِكَةِ

679
00:48:04,325 --> 00:48:09,658
And then Allah made a test and presented some objects on the angels.

680
00:48:10,396 --> 00:48:19,963
فَقَالَ أَنبِـُٔونِى بِأَسْمَاءِ هَـٰؤُلَاءِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَـٰدِقِينَ۝

681
00:48:20,892 --> 00:48:25,935
Tell Me the names of these if you are true. “if you are truthful, if you are right,”

682
00:48:26,142 --> 00:48:29,293
because the angels, they said at the beginning;

683
00:48:29,333 --> 00:48:34,055
“Why are You going to create a human being who will cause bloodshed and corruption?”

684
00:48:34,444 --> 00:48:39,007
Allah سبحانه وتعالى made this test and told the angels to identify these objects.

685
00:48:39,110 --> 00:48:40,253
What did the angels say?

686
00:48:40,451 --> 00:48:54,031
قَالُوا سُبْحَـٰنَكَ لَا عِلْمَ لَنَا إِلَّا مَا عَلَّمْتَنَا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ۝

687
00:48:54,200 --> 00:48:55,192
They said;

688
00:48:55,721 --> 00:49:01,991
“Glory be to You, we have no knowledge but the knowledge that You have given us.”

689
00:49:02,738 --> 00:49:03,841
إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ۝

690
00:49:03,881 --> 00:49:07,293
 You are the Most Knowledgeable and the All-Wise.

691
00:49:08,405 --> 00:49:11,805
And now it’s Adam(آدم‎)’s turn to go through the test.

692
00:49:12,297 --> 00:49:19,553
قَالَ يَـٰـَٔادَمُ أَنبِئْهُم بِأَسْمَائِهِمْ

693
00:49:19,736 --> 00:49:23,347
O Adam(آدَم), tell them these names.

694
00:49:23,847 --> 00:49:25,275
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

695
00:49:25,601 --> 00:49:34,433
فَلَمَّا أَنبَأَهُم بِأَسْمَائِهِمْ قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ

696
00:49:34,680 --> 00:49:42,210
أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ إِنِّى أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ ٱلسَّمَـٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ

697
00:49:42,345 --> 00:49:50,198
وَأَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُونَ وَمَا كُنتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ۝

698
00:49:50,634 --> 00:49:55,022
And when he told them the names, Allah سبحانه وتعالى told the angels;

699
00:49:55,062 --> 00:49:59,892
Didn’t I tell you that I know the knowledge of the Unseen in the heavens and the earth

700
00:50:00,091 --> 00:50:04,000
and I know what you reveal and what you conceal.

701
00:50:04,040 --> 00:50:05,982
Allah سبحانه وتعالى knows all knowledge.

702
00:50:06,197 --> 00:50:10,742
So Allah is telling the angels there is a hikmah(حكمة‎) for the creation of Adam(آدم‎) you don't know.

703
00:50:11,560 --> 00:50:14,163
There is a hikmah(حكمة‎)‎ that you don't know,

704
00:50:14,472 --> 00:50:20,573
and that is a lesson for us whenever we see something that we’re not able to understand or comprehend.

705
00:50:20,613 --> 00:50:22,987
We need to understand that Allah has a wisdom behind it.

706
00:50:23,939 --> 00:50:27,421
There is a hikmah(حكمة‎), there is a wisdom behind every action.

707
00:50:28,810 --> 00:50:30,294
There is a hikmah(حكمة‎) behind everything

708
00:50:30,683 --> 00:50:36,536
because many times human beings fall into that trap of questioning why some events are happening.

709
00:50:36,711 --> 00:50:39,409
I mean, “Why is this happening?” And we question Qadr(قدر)

710
00:50:39,592 --> 00:50:45,752
and we question misery and we question disease and we question disasters and we question wars.

711
00:50:45,943 --> 00:50:47,570
“Why are these things happening?”

712
00:50:48,316 --> 00:50:52,916
We need to realize Allah has a wisdom in everything that is happening around us, there is a reason.

713
00:50:53,537 --> 00:50:55,608
We don't know it, Allah سبحانه وتعالى knows it.

714
00:50:56,926 --> 00:50:58,412
So that's the story of the names.

715
00:50:59,586 --> 00:51:00,801
Adam(آدم‎) was alone.

716
00:51:01,539 --> 00:51:03,066
هُوَ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَكُم مِّن نَّفْسٍ وَٰحِدَةٍ

717
00:51:03,106 --> 00:51:08,343
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says you were created from one self, one nafs(نفس), one soul

718
00:51:09,143 --> 00:51:10,366
and that is Adam(آدم‎).

719
00:51:12,056 --> 00:51:17,553
And then Allah سبحانه وتعالى created out of Adam(آدم‎) his mate, Hawa(هوى‎).

720
00:51:18,299 --> 00:51:24,432
And then the hadith(حديث‎) tells us that Hawa(هوى‎) was created from the rib of Sayyiduna Adam(سيدنا آدم‎).

721
00:51:25,337 --> 00:51:26,813
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

722
00:51:27,448 --> 00:51:38,404
يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ ٱتَّقُوا۟ رَبَّكُمُ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَكُم مِّن نَّفْسٍ وَٰحِدَةٍ

723
00:51:38,610 --> 00:51:41,561
وَخَلَقَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا

724
00:51:41,624 --> 00:51:50,272
وَبَثَّ مِنْهُمَا رِجَالًا كَثِيرًا وَنِسَآءً ۚ

725
00:51:50,367 --> 00:51:58,176
وَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِى تَسَآءَلُونَ بِهِۦ وَٱلْأَرْحَامَ ۚ

726
00:51:58,291 --> 00:52:04,005
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَيْكُمْ رَقِيبًا۝

727
00:52:04,069 --> 00:52:08,191
O mankind, be dutiful to your Lord who created you from a single person,

728
00:52:08,445 --> 00:52:14,128
and from him He created his wife, and from them both He created many men and women.

729
00:52:14,223 --> 00:52:15,900
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث);

730
00:52:16,146 --> 00:52:17,583
استوصوا بالنساء خيرا

731
00:52:18,622 --> 00:52:21,241
فإن المرأة خلقت من ضلع

732
00:52:22,090 --> 00:52:24,763
وإن أعوج شيء في الضلع أعلاه

733
00:52:24,993 --> 00:52:31,950
فإن ذهبت تقيمه كسرته وإن تركته لم يزل أعوج فاستوصوا بالنساء خيرا

734
00:52:32,022 --> 00:52:32,895
متفق عليه

735
00:52:33,379 --> 00:52:37,910
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: “Take good care of women.

736
00:52:38,680 --> 00:52:41,046
Women were created from a rib,

737
00:52:41,356 --> 00:52:45,459
and the most bent part of the rib is the top of it.

738
00:52:46,332 --> 00:52:49,591
If you try to make it straight, you'll break it,

739
00:52:49,817 --> 00:52:54,079
and if you leave it, it’ll remain bent, so take good care of women.

740
00:52:54,849 --> 00:53:00,626
If we understand this hadith(حديث‎), the communication between men and women would be much better and easier.

741
00:53:01,491 --> 00:53:04,859
Adam(آدم‎) and Hawa(هوى‎) were living in Jannah(جنة).

742
00:53:05,456 --> 00:53:13,544
They had all of Jannah(جنة‎), but there was an exception and that is the tree.

743
00:53:13,774 --> 00:53:16,675
One tree, now what type of tree is this?

744
00:53:17,433 --> 00:53:23,416
Apple tree? Banana tree? Asking this question, to start with, is part of

745
00:53:23,456 --> 00:53:24,812
علم لا ينفع

746
00:53:25,162 --> 00:53:26,717
knowledge that does not benefit.

747
00:53:27,424 --> 00:53:34,083
Going into this is part of the knowledge that does not benefit and that's why Allah سبحانه وتعالى did not mention it in Qur’an.

748
00:53:35,774 --> 00:53:43,016
The details of these stories are not mentioned in Qur’an - what type of tree was it, what’s the name of it, how long it was.

749
00:53:43,167 --> 00:53:45,882
I mean, just like for example, in the story of the people of the cave,

750
00:53:46,278 --> 00:53:50,610
to show you that Allah سبحانه وتعالى is telling us about knowledge that would benefit us

751
00:53:50,650 --> 00:53:54,770
but sometimes we try to go into areas that would not benefit us.

752
00:53:55,135 --> 00:53:56,914
Allah سبحانه وتعالى left it

753
00:53:57,342 --> 00:54:00,207
and we try to go and investigate(wrong practice).

754
00:54:00,636 --> 00:54:04,218
In the story of the young men, when they went in the cave,

755
00:54:04,406 --> 00:54:06,557
وَكَلْبُهُم بَـٰسِطٌ ذِرَاعَيْهِ بِٱلْوَصِيدِ

756
00:54:06,779 --> 00:54:11,782
It says that their dog was spreading its arms on the entrance of the cave.

757
00:54:12,335 --> 00:54:15,013
Some started questioning: “what type of dog was it”?

758
00:54:15,299 --> 00:54:16,561
and “what’s the color of the dog”?

759
00:54:16,648 --> 00:54:21,682
Some of them said: “It's white” and some of them said: “It’s black” and some of them said: “No, it’s a mixture of black and white.”

760
00:54:22,031 --> 00:54:25,428
I mean, what kind of benefit can we learn from this knowledge? Nothing.

761
00:54:26,809 --> 00:54:31,996
The reason why these stories are mentioned in Qur’an are not as a historical account,

762
00:54:32,175 --> 00:54:34,325
but they are mentioned for their Ibrah(عبرة).

763
00:54:35,206 --> 00:54:36,143
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

764
00:54:36,183 --> 00:54:37,368
لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ

765
00:54:37,408 --> 00:54:40,772
So that they may contemplate.

766
00:54:41,185 --> 00:54:42,238
And Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

767
00:54:42,278 --> 00:54:44,454
عِبْرَةٌ لِّأُولِى ٱلْأَلْبَـٰابِ

768
00:54:44,494 --> 00:54:46,871
These are lessons for the ones of understanding.

769
00:54:47,331 --> 00:54:50,474
So the tree was mentioned in Qur’an;

770
00:54:50,499 --> 00:54:51,154
شَجَرَةِ ٱلْخُلْدِ

771
00:54:51,305 --> 00:54:52,646
It’s just a tree,

772
00:54:53,353 --> 00:54:58,670
but we do not know what kind of tree was it and where it was and how tall it was…

773
00:54:59,234 --> 00:55:00,217
we don’t know those details.

774
00:55:00,336 --> 00:55:01,193
It was a tree

775
00:55:01,534 --> 00:55:05,598
that is the only part of Jannah(جنة‎) Adam(آدم‎) and Hawa(هوى‎) were not supposed to touch.

776
00:55:06,669 --> 00:55:08,009
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

777
00:55:08,336 --> 00:55:15,066
وَقُلْنَا يَـٰـَٔادَمُ ٱسْكُنْ أَنتَ وَزَوْجُكَ ٱلْجَنَّةَ

778
00:55:15,248 --> 00:55:19,989
وَكُلَا مِنْهَا رَغَدًا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمَا

779
00:55:20,076 --> 00:55:27,268
 وَلَا تَقْرَبَا هَـٰذِهِ ٱلشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونَا مِنَ ٱلظَّـٰلِمِينَ۝

780
00:55:27,308 --> 00:55:35,028
And We said: O Adam(آدَم), live, and your mate, in Jannah(جنة) and eat from it wherever you want,

781
00:55:35,282 --> 00:55:37,337
but do not touch this tree.

782
00:55:37,853 --> 00:55:39,147
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

783
00:55:39,227 --> 00:55:41,200
فَوَسْوَسَ إِلَيْهِ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنُ

784
00:55:41,724 --> 00:55:44,763
Shaitan(شيطان) gave Adam(آدم‎) waswasah(وسوسة).

785
00:55:45,001 --> 00:55:52,016
Waswasah(وسوسة) is some hidden speech that he’s delivering in one's mind, evil inspiration.

786
00:55:53,000 --> 00:55:55,778
What did Iblis(إبليس), Shaytan(شيطان) tell Adam (آدم‎)?

787
00:55:56,643 --> 00:55:59,302
Did he tell Adam(آدم‎): “Go and eat from the tree Allah told you: ‘Don't touch’”?

788
00:56:00,524 --> 00:56:03,821
Did he tell Adam(آدم‎): “Go and disobey Allah سبحانه وتعالى”?

789
00:56:04,599 --> 00:56:06,702
Did he tell him: “Go and commit Haram(حرام)”?

790
00:56:08,226 --> 00:56:10,742
He knew how to deal with the human being.

791
00:56:10,941 --> 00:56:14,256
فَوَسْوَسَ إِلَيْهِ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنُ

792
00:56:14,336 --> 00:56:20,698
قَالَ يَـٰـَٔادَمُ هَلْ أَدُلُّكَ عَلَىٰ شَجَرَةِ ٱلْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَّا يَبْلَىٰ

793
00:56:21,372 --> 00:56:27,468
He said: Shall I tell you about the tree that will give you infinite life, eternity,

794
00:56:28,111 --> 00:56:33,167
and will give you the greatest kingdom that will not end?

795
00:56:34,024 --> 00:56:38,873
Shaytan(شيطان) knows our points of weakness and that's where he attacks from.

796
00:56:39,961 --> 00:56:41,778
He didn't go to Adam(آدم‎) bluntly and tell him;

797
00:56:41,818 --> 00:56:44,723
“Go and disobey Allah سبحانه وتعالى.” Otherwise, Adam(آدم‎) wouldn't have done it.

798
00:56:45,207 --> 00:56:50,009
He told him: This tree would give you continuous life, eternal life,

799
00:56:50,159 --> 00:56:51,644
and it would give you kingdom.

800
00:56:52,366 --> 00:56:57,606
Adam(آدم‎) and Hawa(هوى‎) - they ate from that tree, and because of that, Allah سبحانه وتعالى sent them down to Earth.

801
00:56:59,217 --> 00:57:01,741
Whenever you read this Ayah(آية) or hear about this story,

802
00:57:01,781 --> 00:57:09,055
do you ever wonder how could such a great Nabi(نبي) commit such a mistake?

803
00:57:09,579 --> 00:57:14,901
Do you ever wonder how come Allah سبحانه وتعالى told him: “Don't touch from that tree”

804
00:57:14,941 --> 00:57:16,639
and then he went and ate from it?

805
00:57:17,956 --> 00:57:19,837
Do you ever wonder how could that happen?

806
00:57:21,075 --> 00:57:24,432
I think some of you may had that idea.

807
00:57:24,721 --> 00:57:27,265
How come, this is a Nabi(نبي) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى, how could he do that?

808
00:57:27,345 --> 00:57:29,085
By the way, at that time, he was not a Nabi(نبي) yet,

809
00:57:29,482 --> 00:57:31,497
but later in Earth, he became of the Ambiya(أنبياء‎).

810
00:57:33,990 --> 00:57:36,651
Instead of thinking about why Adam(آدم‎) did so,

811
00:57:37,571 --> 00:57:41,908
why not think about yourself that you are committing sins and mistakes.

812
00:57:42,175 --> 00:57:49,973
 It is much more difficult to understand how we can commit sins

813
00:57:50,695 --> 00:57:54,476
because, with Adam(آدم‎), he did not have any experience whatsoever;

814
00:57:54,714 --> 00:57:59,901
he did not know about Shaytan(شيطان), he had only knowledge about Shaytan(شيطان), but he had no experience with him.

815
00:58:00,877 --> 00:58:02,485
An experience is different than knowledge.

816
00:58:02,559 --> 00:58:07,908
With Adam(آدم‎), he knew that Shaytan(شيطان) is his enemy, but he never experienced it.

817
00:58:08,527 --> 00:58:09,916
And even Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

818
00:58:09,956 --> 00:58:12,001
ليس الخبر كالمعاينة

819
00:58:12,588 --> 00:58:14,997
 “Knowing the news is not like seeing it.”

820
00:58:15,628 --> 00:58:19,510
Adam(آدم‎) had the knowledge, but he didn't have any experience with Shaytan(شيطان) yet.

821
00:58:20,296 --> 00:58:24,598
We know what happened to Adam(آدم‎) and we know it was caused by Shaytan(شيطان)

822
00:58:24,876 --> 00:58:31,140
and we have seen a long history, of mankind and we’re still committing the same mistake again and again.

823
00:58:32,648 --> 00:58:36,854
We should question that, we should not question the fact that Adam(آدم‎) committed this mistake

824
00:58:37,795 --> 00:58:40,311
because for Adam(آدم‎), it was a very innocent mistake,

825
00:58:41,382 --> 00:58:43,309
and Allah سبحانه وتعالى forgave him

826
00:58:44,444 --> 00:58:50,171
because Adam(آدم‎) did not have any experience yet and Allah سبحانه وتعالى wanted this to be a test for Adam(آدم‎)

827
00:58:50,298 --> 00:58:55,395
so that he could learn from it and this could be experience for Adam(آدم‎) to prepare him

828
00:58:55,435 --> 00:58:57,834
because he will be a Nabi(نبي) of Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

829
00:58:58,501 --> 00:59:01,338
It's a preparation for Adam(آدم‎); Allah’s preparing him

830
00:59:01,529 --> 00:59:06,688
just like Allah سبحانه وتعالى was preparing Dawud(داود) through the mistake that he committed and we’re gonna talk about that.

831
00:59:06,979 --> 00:59:10,257
Allah سبحانه وتعالى was preparing Dawud(داود) for the position of Khilafah(خلافة‎)

832
00:59:10,392 --> 00:59:13,798
so Allah سبحانه وتعالى made him go through that judgment and he made a mistake in it

833
00:59:14,068 --> 00:59:16,648
and then Allah سبحانه وتعالى corrected that mistake for him.

834
00:59:16,838 --> 00:59:20,195
They say that Dawud(داود), after the mistake, was better than he was before.

835
00:59:21,092 --> 00:59:26,703
So Allah سبحانه وتعالى was preparing Adam(آدم‎) so that he would go through this experience and learn from it

836
00:59:27,020 --> 00:59:32,747
and it would prepare him for living on this earth to realize that Shaytan(شيطان), Iblis(إبليس), is your enemy.

837
00:59:33,659 --> 00:59:35,199
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

838
00:59:35,477 --> 00:59:40,299
وَقُلْنَا ٱهْبِطُوا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ

839
00:59:40,545 --> 00:59:44,632
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says: Get you down, all.

840
00:59:46,124 --> 00:59:51,371
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told Adam(آدم‎) and Hawa(هوى‎) to get out of Jannah(جنة‎).

841
00:59:51,918 --> 01:00:01,978
In Arabic, there is singular, which is for one, and then there is another form for two and then there is plural for three and more.

842
01:00:02,200 --> 01:00:05,132
In English, we have only singular and plural;

843
01:00:05,489 --> 01:00:08,783
singular is for one, plural is for how many?

844
01:00:09,727 --> 01:00:10,346
Two or more.

845
01:00:10,561 --> 01:00:14,936
In English, if you are talking about two people, you say “they”. You don’t say “he”.

846
01:00:15,261 --> 01:00:15,849
“They”

847
01:00:16,388 --> 01:00:17,047
it’s two of them.

848
01:00:17,277 --> 01:00:21,707
But in Arabic, plural is not 2, plural is three or more.

849
01:00:22,106 --> 01:00:25,075
There is another form that is used for the two.

850
01:00:26,432 --> 01:00:28,233
Adam(آدم‎) and Hawa(هوى‎) are two.

851
01:00:29,091 --> 01:00:32,078
Allah سبحانه وتعالى referred to them in the plural form.

852
01:00:32,118 --> 01:00:32,854
 ٱهْبِطُوا۟

853
01:00:33,078 --> 01:00:33,904
All of you…

854
01:00:33,944 --> 01:00:37,285
All of you descend down from Jannah(جنة) in a plural form…

855
01:00:37,325 --> 01:00:38,559
but they were only two.

856
01:00:39,988 --> 01:00:43,868
Al-Farah(الفرح) says, one of the Mufassireen(مفسرين‎), he says;

857
01:00:44,122 --> 01:00:48,696
Because this command is to Adam(آدم‎) and his wife and all of us with them.

858
01:00:49,609 --> 01:00:53,228
All of us were in Jannah(جنة‎), that's where we were.

859
01:00:53,514 --> 01:00:58,347
But because of Iblis(إبليس) and Shaytan(شيطان) and that mistake, we all came down to Duniya(دنيا‎).

860
01:00:58,720 --> 01:01:00,530
So we do not really belong to Duniya(دنيا‎)

861
01:01:00,934 --> 01:01:02,473
this is not where we belong to.

862
01:01:02,513 --> 01:01:05,854
We are here for a temporary time, we belong to Al-Akhirah(الآخرة‎).

863
01:01:08,188 --> 01:01:11,324
وَلَكُمْ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَمَتَـٰعٌ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ۝

864
01:01:11,364 --> 01:01:15,149
On Earth will be a dwelling place for you and an enjoyment for a time.

865
01:01:15,189 --> 01:01:16,741
You’re gonna stay there for a while.

866
01:01:18,217 --> 01:01:21,122
Allah سبحانه وتعالى taught Adam(آدم‎) some words to learn.

867
01:01:21,534 --> 01:01:28,487
فَتَلَقَّىٰ ءَادَمُ مِن رَّبِّهِۦ كَلِمَـٰتٍ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ ۚ

868
01:01:28,749 --> 01:01:33,236
إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلتَّوَّابُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ۝

869
01:01:33,505 --> 01:01:40,649
Then Adam(آدَم) received from his Lord words, and His Lord pardoned him and accepted his repentance.

870
01:01:40,840 --> 01:01:43,054
Verily, He is the One who forgives.

871
01:01:43,665 --> 01:01:50,845
So Allah taught Adam(آدم‎) words to say, Allah taught Adam(آدم‎) a Dua(دُعَا) to say, and then Allah سبحانه وتعالى forgave him.

872
01:01:50,948 --> 01:01:52,297
What was this Dua(دُعَا)?

873
01:01:52,599 --> 01:01:58,398
قَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَا أَنفُسَنَا

874
01:01:58,612 --> 01:02:06,561
وَإِن لَّمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا لَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْخَـٰسِرِينَ۝

875
01:02:06,641 --> 01:02:08,235
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

876
01:02:08,743 --> 01:02:12,922
They said: Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves.

877
01:02:13,246 --> 01:02:20,566
If You forgive us not and bestow not upon us Your mercy, we shall certainly be of the losers.

878
01:02:22,034 --> 01:02:23,915
We have wronged ourselves. Look at this Dua(دُعَا),

879
01:02:24,248 --> 01:02:29,157
very important Dua(دُعَا), and please memorize it and use it because it is the Duʿa(دعاء) of the sinners.

880
01:02:30,863 --> 01:02:32,141
رَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَا أَنفُسَنَا

881
01:02:32,839 --> 01:02:35,188
O Allah, we have wronged ourselves, we have committed wrong

882
01:02:35,768 --> 01:02:40,417
and we have harmed ourselves by this wrong, we’re not harming Allah, we’re harming our own selves.

883
01:02:41,615 --> 01:02:43,980
وَإِن لَّمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا

884
01:02:44,020 --> 01:02:49,057
If You do not have forgiveness on us and mercy, we would be of the losers.

885
01:02:51,176 --> 01:02:54,215
If you do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we would be losers.

886
01:02:54,311 --> 01:02:58,898
We need You, O Allah, so please, O Allah, we beg You to forgive us and have mercy on us.

887
01:02:59,382 --> 01:03:03,206
This is the Duʿa(دعاء) that Allah سبحانه وتعالى taught Adam(آدم‎) and Hawa(هوى‎).

888
01:03:04,548 --> 01:03:07,183
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

